Windows XP TTY SlashEM Version 0.0.7E6F2

In Minetown I accidentally picked up a loadstone (it was in a chest in a 
shop). I know i t is a loadstone because I have SHOW_WEIGHT on and my 
weight went up by 500.
I tried to drop it and I got the usual 'you cant drop this stone' message.
I went to the temple, stripped off everything except armour,weapon and 
lodestone.Dropped all non-essentials and went to the fountain outside 
Izchak's shop.
I started #dipping the lodestone in the fountain, hoping to get a nymph.
Water gushed out of the fountain and drowned Izchak. (oops!)

I went to the other fountain and started dipping again.
On an impulse, I tried dropping the lodestone again.To my great 
surprise, it did drop. "you see here a cursed grey stone".
I saved, backed up in case of a crash, and went back in the game.
I picked up the stone, went to a shop and got it identified.It was 
Identified as a cursed flint stone!
However it still increases my weight by 500, even though it is supposed 
to be a flintstone.
I remember hearing about a loadstone bug, but ISTR that it was quite a 
while ago and that it involved corrupting your inventory.
Can anyone give a full description of the lodestone bug?

